cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AquaContam: An ML Benchmark for Predicting PFAS and Heavy Metal Contamination in U.S. Drinking Water"
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 4.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22073200
date-released: '2026-08-24'
abstract: >-
  AquaContam is a machine learning benchmark for predicting PFAS and heavy metal
  contamination in U.S. public drinking water systems. It integrates EPA monitoring
  data with geospatial features and provides standardized tasks, geographic splits,
  and equity analysis tools for reproducible environmental health research.
url: "https://github.com/tjnewton/aquacontam"
